<p>The build-up to this one is quite enjoyable, with tension rising as the archeologist's race for the truth and the various historical accounts begin to reveal more and more about what exactly is going on. And then we get to that twist.</p>
<p>I really love WJS's 001 proposal. To me, it is highly plausible and has fantastic narrative potential (and that letter from the 05 at the end). The revelation here that the O5 council have basically made a ruling on what is anomalous on such a grand scale as to condemn everything that isn't the actual anomalies takes the WJS 001 idea to an interesting extreme that it makes me pause and reflect on the nature of that 001.</p>
<p>This was a fun article, and I am glad you got it up in time, M_E.</p>
<p>+1.</p>

