			<div class="content" id="post-content-3897673">
									

<p>I absolutely love this. The resonating tie-ins are so far-reaching, so complete, and so comprehensive.</p>
<p>It requires a really in-depth knowledge of the Foundation *and* at least a cursory knowledge of real myth to fully distinguish what's going on. For my part, I definitely thought there was more going on with the whole &quot;I cannot bear an heir&quot; thing, more than Etana just literally being unable to conceive children, until I researched it and realize that was part of the real epic.</p>
<p>It's a bit of obscuring opaqueness to what's going on that might make some people miss the &quot;punchline&quot; so to speak, but you might be okay with it - it makes picking through this like picking through the symbolism of old real-world myths to suss what's actually going on.</p>
<p>All in all though, it's a weighty piece that beautifully fulfills the history theme, makes my brain happy, and makes my heart excited.</p>
<p>I hope this goes far.</p>

							</div>

								
					
